# Continuous workflow orchestrator

**Chief agent** (coordination) sits above a **polling orchestrator** (ship bar). Parent agents spawn **chief first**; chief delegates orchestrator cycles.

## Session start

If dirty `git status`, open `gh pr list`, or recent subagent work — **spawn chief first** unless waived. Chief delegates orchestrator for git/PR work.

**Manual orchestrator invoke** (`run workflow orchestrator`) when chief waived or already delegated this turn.

## After substantive subagent work

1. Spawn or resume **chief** unless in flight or waived.
2. Chief re-scans and delegates orchestrator or path owners.
3. When executing orchestrator yourself, follow `~/.cursor/skills/workflow-orchestrator/SKILL.md`.

## One PR per task (hard)

- **Do not** bundle unrelated features, docs, and infra in one PR.
- Partition by disjoint file sets; one branch per logical task.
- Meta workflow plumbing stays its own PR.

## Babysit pairing

For open PR review / CI / bot threads, delegate to **Cursor built-in babysit skill** (`babysit/SKILL.md`) with one worker per PR number.

## Ship bar

Orchestrator coordinates `WORKFLOW.md` steps 5–7 (bot wait, synthesis, thread closure) and project-specific steps 8–9 (`{DEPLOY_COMMAND}`, `{VERIFY_COMMAND}`). Does **not** waive closeout gates.

## Manual invoke

**"run workflow orchestrator"** — read orchestrator skill and run SCAN→PLAN→DELEGATE.
